  "candidate_answer_audit": "The candidate answer (clean-based ulcer) is strongly supported by the Forrest classification, which defines clean-based ulcer (Forrest III) as having the lowest rebleeding risk after initial hemostasis. This aligns with standard GI bleeding management guidelines. The clinical stability and unchanged hematocrit further support that rebleeding is unlikely without intervention. Therefore, the candidate is well-supported by evidence.",
